{
  "explanation": "The attacker utilized the automated vulnerability scanner Nuclei from IP 193.106.191.50 to systematically probe the web server for sensitive files and administrative endpoints, such as Git repositories, backup archives, and configuration backups. The HTTP 404 status codes returned in the logs indicate that the targeted resources were not found on the server, meaning this specific reconnaissance attempt was unsuccessful at locating exposed assets.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Reconnaissance",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Block the source IP address (193.106.191.50) at the firewall or WAF level.",
    "Implement rate limiting and bot detection mechanisms to mitigate automated scanning tools like Nuclei.",
    "Ensure that sensitive configuration files, backup archives, and version control directories (.git) are strictly excluded from public web root deployments."
  ]
}
